uals ``digest`` (a 64-character hex string).","end":306,"hash":"a2b3d9f244","kind":"function","loc":6,"name":"fingerprint_matches","params":[{"name":"root"},{"name":"digest"},{"name":"**limits"}],"qual":"fingerprint_matches","returns":"bool","start":301,"test":false,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":306,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-11-14"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-11-14","last":"2026-11-14"},"lang":"python","lines":306,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/fingerprint.py -- Patch C26: a fingerprint of everything in a project folder that can change what the\nagent is allowed or told to do.\n\nWhy\n---\nA project folder is attacker-controlled content (a cloned repository), and a few of its files are *configuration with power*:\nsettings that can allow commands without asking, hooks that run commands, skills that add instructions the model follows.\nA person's decision \"I trust this folder\" must therefore be tied to the exact bytes of those files, so that a ``git pull``\nwhich edits a hook is a NEW question, not an old answer.  This module computes the thing the decision is tied to.\n\nWhat is covered (and nothing else)\n----------------------------------\n    .m2c/settings.toml       the project settings\n    .m2c/rules/**            project rules\n    .m2c/hooks/**            hooks (they will live here, or in settings.toml)\n    .m2c/skills/**           project skills\n    .agents/skills/**        project skills (cross-tool location)\n    .claude/skills/**        project skills (Claude-style location)\n\nFiles anywhere else (source code, README, ``.m2c/checkpoints``, ``.claude/commands`` ...) change nothing here.  Two limits\nworth knowing: the digest does not include file modes (the bytes decide what is configured), and trusting a hook that runs\n``./scripts/x.sh`` trusts the configuration, not whatever that script later becomes -- the same as any command a person\nputs in a config file.  Instruction files (``M2C.md``, ``AGENTS.md`","path":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/fingerprint.py","size":13378,"test":false},{"binary":false,"blank":26,"classes":[{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":true,"doc1":"Nothing is decided; ``message`` (maybe empty) is a hint to show.","end":44,"fields":[{"name":"message","type":"str"}],"hash":"34d1d7534e","loc":4,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"Pending","qual":"Pending","start":41},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":true,"doc1":"``trust``: use the project's settings now.","end":52,"fields":[{"name":"trust","type":"bool"},{"name":"remember","type":"bool"}],"hash":"d485f325ba","loc":5,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"Answer","qual":"Answer","start":48},{"bases":[],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"One question, one answer.","end":83,"hash":"362d84aef1","loc":26,"method_names":["__init__","done","feed"],"methods":3,"name":"TrustPromptMachine","qual":"TrustPromptMachine","start":58}],"code":85,"comment":24,"exports":["Answer","MAX_FILES_SHOWN","Pending","TrustPromptMachine","describe_prompt","ignored_note"],"ext":"py","functions":[{"args":2,"async":false,"cc":1,"cc_deep":1,"code":3,"decorators":[],"doc":false,"end":63,"hash":"6c175168a4","kind":"method","loc":3,"name":"__init__","params":[{"name":"self"},{"annotation":"TrustState","name":"state"}],"qual":"TrustPromptMachine.__init__","returns":"None","start":61,"test":false,"visibility":"dunder"},{"args":1,"async":false,"cc":1,"cc_deep":1,"code":2,"decorators":["property"],"doc":false,"end":67,"hash":"4e0e93f7a8","kind":"method","loc":2,"name":"done","params":[{"name":"self"}],"qual":"TrustPromptMachine.done","returns":"bool","start":66,"test":false,"visibility":"public"},{"args":2,"async":false,"calls":[["Pending","m2c/src/m2c/trust/prompt.py::Pending"],["Answer","m2c/src/m2c/trust/prompt.py::Answer"]],"cc":11,"cc_deep":11,"code":15,"decorators":[],"doc":false,"end":83,"hash":"99448a91a1","kind":"method","loc":15,"name":"feed","params":[{"name":"self"},{"annotation":"object","name":"key"}],"qual":"TrustPromptMachine.feed","returns":"Step","start":69,"test":false,"visibility":"public"},{"args":1,"async":false,"calls":[["line","m2c/src/m2c/tui/render.py::line"],["clean_line","m2c/src/m2c/tui/safe.py::clean_line"]],"cc":5,"cc_deep":5,"code":27,"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The prompt, as display lines (short enough not to wrap in an ordinary terminal, except the folder name).","end":113,"hash":"aa25f19056","kind":"function","loc":28,"name":"describe_prompt","params":[{"annotation":"TrustState","name":"state"}],"qual":"describe_prompt","returns":"list[Block]","start":86,"test":false,"visibility":"public"},{"args":1,"async":false,"cc":8,"cc_deep":8,"code":19,"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The one status line for a folder whose project files are not used, or None when there is nothing to say.","end":135,"hash":"3caa16955a","kind":"function","loc":20,"name":"ignored_note","params":[{"annotation":"TrustState","name":"state"}],"qual":"ignored_note","returns":"Optional[str]","start":116,"test":false,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":135,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-11-14"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-11-14","last":"2026-11-14"},"lang":"python","lines":135,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/prompt.py -- Patch C26: the folder-trust prompt as a pure key state machine, what it shows, and the status\nnote for a folder that is not trusted.\n\nLike tui/approval.py, this is the pure part: what the prompt shows (``describe_prompt``), what each key means\n(``TrustPromptMachine``), and the one-line note (``ignored_note``).  The terminal layer (tui/session.py) only forwards keys\nand shows blocks.\n\nKEYS\n----\n``t`` trust this folder and remember it (until its files change) · ``s`` trust it for this session only, remember nothing ·\n``n`` do not trust it, and remember that (until its files change) · Esc the same as ``n``.  Any other key does nothing: no\nkey ever answers by accident (Enter, Space and Tab included), and the machine answers at most once.  Closing m2c with the\nquestion open answers nothing and remembers nothing, so the person is asked again next time.\n\nWHAT IS SHOWN\n-------------\nThe folder, how many files and which (the names come from the project, so every one is cleaned of terminal control\ncharacters and cut), a plain-language warning, and the keys.  The list is cut at MAX_FILES_SHOWN names with a count of the rest.\n\nStandard library plus the display helpers of tui/render.py and tui/safe.py (no terminal library, no I/O).\n\nPlace this file at: m2c/src/m2c/trust/prompt.py","path":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/prompt.py","size":5997,"test":false},{"binary":false,"blank":46,"classes":[{"bases":["Exception"],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The trust file cannot be used.","end":97,"hash":"e899550eba","loc":2,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"TrustStoreError","qual":"TrustStoreError","start":96},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":false,"end":104,"fields":[{"name":"decision","type":"str"},{"name":"fingerprint","type":"str"},{"name":"time","type":"int"}],"hash":"a7fba749ca","loc":4,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"TrustEntry","qual":"TrustEntry","start":101},{"bases":[],"decorators":["dataclass(frozen=True)"],"doc":false,"end":115,"fields":[{"name":"root","type":"str"},{"name":"trusted","type":"bool"},{"name":"needs_prompt","type":"bool"},{"name":"files","type":"tuple[str, ...]"},{"name":"reason","type":"str"},{"name":"fingerprint","type":"Optional[str]"},{"name":"message","type":"str"}],"hash":"866f56b191","loc":8,"method_names":[],"methods":0,"name":"TrustState","qual":"TrustState","start":108},{"bases":[],"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The trust file.","end":323,"hash":"ae825a4639","loc":176,"method_names":["__init__","default","_fail","_read","_damaged","load","get","items","set","forget","_write","_sync_dir"],"methods":12,"name":"TrustStore","qual":"TrustStore","start":148}],"code":251,"comment":67,"exports":["DECISIONS","FILE_NAME","MAX_ENTRIES","MAX_FILE_BYTES","REASONS","TrustEntry","TrustS