s":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"The trust decision for a project folder (see the module docstring).","end":350,"hash":"b55b287890","kind":"function","loc":25,"name":"project_trust_state","params":[{"name":"root"},{"annotation":"TrustStore","name":"store"},{"name":"**limits"}],"qual":"project_trust_state","returns":"TrustState","start":326,"test":false,"visibility":"public"},{"args":5,"async":false,"calls":[["TrustState","m2c/src/m2c/trust/store.py::TrustState"],["log_event","m2c/src/m2c/logging_setup.py::log_event"]],"cc":1,"cc_deep":1,"code":12,"decorators":[],"doc":false,"end":364,"hash":"4012490ec6","kind":"function","loc":12,"name":"_state","params":[{"annotation":"str","name":"root"},{"annotation":"str","name":"reason"},{"name":"files"},{"name":"fingerprint"},{"annotation":"str","default":"''","name":"message"}],"qual":"_state","returns":"TrustState","start":353,"test":false,"visibility":"private"}],"git":{"added":364,"commits":1,"dates":["2026-11-14"],"deleted":0,"first":"2026-11-14","last":"2026-11-14"},"lang":"python","lines":364,"module_doc":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/store.py -- Patch C26: the folder-trust store (``<M2C home>/trust.json``) and the trust decision.\n\nWhat is stored\n--------------\nOne small JSON file mapping the CANONICAL absolute project root (its real path, so a symlinked path and the real path are the\nsame folder) to what the person decided and for which files:\n\n    {\"version\": 1,\n     \"folders\": {\"/home/me/code/app\": {\"decision\": \"trusted\" | \"untrusted\",\n                                       \"fingerprint\": \"<64 hex, see fingerprint.py>\",\n                                       \"time\": <seconds since the epoch>}}}\n\nA decision is only ever valid for the fingerprint it was made for.  Any change to a trust-relevant file (a ``git pull`` that\nedits a hook, say) changes the fingerprint, so the old answer no longer applies and the person is asked again.  An explicit\n\"untrusted\" is remembered the same way, so the person is not asked again for the same files.\n\nHow the file is protected (it is a security file: a forged \"trusted\" entry would switch on a folder's hooks)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n* It lives in the M2C home (mode 0700, tightened by ``paths.ensure_config_dir``), created 0600, written atomically: a temp file\n  in the same directory (mode 0600 from the start), flushed and fsynced, then renamed over the old file.  A crash leaves the old\n  file or the new one, never half of one.\n* Reading REFUSES a file that is not a regular file","path":"m2c/src/m2c/trust/store.py","size":17365,"test":false}],"schema":1,"shard":"m2c__src__m2c__trust"}
